Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sat Sep 19 12:50:34 2026 -0500

    fix(install): DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-21 — rule-pack failure skips instead of aborting the base install
    
    On a fresh Debian host without PyYAML, `./install.sh --rule-pack db` printed
    `cannot parse (JSONDecodeError ...)` and exited 2 with NO wrapper installed:
    the opt-in pack phase ran before the base install's mkdir/cp and every
    pack-level refusal ended the whole script under `set -eu`.
    
    New contract — a pack-level failure is a loud SKIP, never an abort:
    
    - PyYAML preflight: when the installed python3 lacks PyYAML, a YAML pack is
      skipped WITHOUT running the validator, naming the missing dependency and
      both remedies (distro python3-yaml / pip install pyyaml). A pack that
      parses as plain JSON still installs through the validator's stdlib-JSON
      fallback — pinned by a new test. Missing python3 entirely: same skip with
      a specific message. The base install (wrapper, lib tree, default rules)
      always completes.
    - Unknown pack name / validator refusal (bad schema, malformed YAML, id
      collision): per-pack loud skip (unknown names suggest --list-rule-packs)
      instead of `exit 2` mid-script. Nothing is written for the skipped pack
      (validate-before-write stays).
    - Exit-code contract: any skipped pack -> final stderr summary (installed:
      wrapper at <path>; skipped entries) and exit 2 at the END. All packs
      installed or none requested: unchanged behavior, exit 0.
    - `--unrule-pack`, POSIX sh, `set -eu`, and fail-closed invariants all kept.
    - rule-pack-tool.py: a no-PyYAML parse failure now names the missing
      dependency instead of surfacing a bare JSONDecodeError (path reachable on
      direct invocations; the installer preflight shows the remedy message).
    
    New battery cells: no-PyYAML host (wrapper present, PyYAML + remedies
    named, no pack file, exit 2), plain-JSON pack installs with PyYAML absent
    (exit 0), no-python3 host, malformed pack with PyYAML present (refused
    pack, wrapper installed, exit 2). Existing "refusal -> exit 2 -> nothing
    installed" expectations deliberately updated to skip-not-abort semantics —
    each marked DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-21 in-test.
    
    Docs: README rule-packs section, docs/quickstart.md, and specs/cli.md
    (installer table + Rule packs section) now document the PyYAML requirement,
    the skip-not-abort behavior, and the exit-code contract.
    
    Addresses DF-TERMINAL-JAIL-21.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
